# What `dart pub publish` leaves out. A .pubignore REPLACES .gitignore for
# pub rather than adding to it, so everything .gitignore names is named here
# again, with its leading `/` kept: an unanchored pattern matches at any
# depth (CLAUDE.md, *.pubignore replaces .gitignore*).
/out/
.dart_tool/
/build/
pubspec.lock
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# The repository's own machinery, which a consumer never runs.
/.github/
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/scripts/
/tool/generate/
/tool/trufflehog/
/tool/pre_push.sh
/CLAUDE.md
/SECURITY.md

# The Flame example's builds and the campaign its prepare step copies in;
# its sources and platform runners are published, as an example should be.
/example/flame_player/build/
/example/flame_player/.dart_tool/
/example/flame_player/assets/campaign/
/example/flame_player/pubspec.lock

/tool/web/
